WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:08.370
As a child Albert Einstein was a slow learner
and spoke very slowly. So much so that his

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:13.540
parents actually feared he may have learning
difficulties. Thankfully, it turned out, that

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:18.820
couldn’t be further from the truth. Here’s
some amazing facts you probably didn’t know

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:23.539
about the man who spearheaded the theory of
relativity and the world’s most renowned

00:00:23.539 --> 00:00:26.289
genius.

00:00:26.289 --> 00:00:36.250
Albert Einstein was born in Ulm in Germany
on 14th March 1879. It is said that the story

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:41.000
of Einstein’s brilliance started when he
was just four years old. His father gave him

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:45.570
a magnetic pocket compass to play with. He
became obsessed with the way the needle seemed

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:51.440
to move around as if by magic. It’s believed
that was the event from where Einstein’s

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:57.620
deep passion for physics originated. Even
as an old man, Einstein wrote about the compass,

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:02.230
saying “I can still remember...that this
experience made a deep and lasting impression

00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:06.560
on me. Something deeply hidden had to be behind
things.”

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:13.020
Einstein became a professor at the Berlin
Academy of Sciences. However, in 1933 he was

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:19.320
visiting America just as Hitler came into
power back in Einstein’s home country of

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:24.610
Germany. Being born to Jewish parents he rightly
thought it would not be a good idea to return

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:29.899
to Germany. The Nazis were so offended by
Einstein’s intellect that they burned all

00:01:29.899 --> 00:01:35.290
his books still remaining in Germany and included
him on a list of enemies of the Nazi state

00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:43.020
entitled “not yet hanged” and put a $5,000
bounty on his head. Einstein responded to

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:49.390
the Nazis by calling their actions a “spontaneous
emotional outburst“ and stating that "more

00:01:49.390 --> 00:01:55.490
than anything else in the world, they fear
the influence of men of intellectual independence."

00:01:55.490 --> 00:02:00.609
Einstein was granted refugee status and became
a citizen of the United States of America,

00:02:00.609 --> 00:02:03.170
where he stayed for the remainder of his life.

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:09.869
Einstein considered himself to be agnostic,
not an atheist. He criticised personal gods,

00:02:09.869 --> 00:02:15.319
i.e. gods that are believed to resemble a
human form. Einstein instead had pantheistic

00:02:15.319 --> 00:02:22.510
beliefs. Which is the idea that the universe
and nature itself, is equal to divinity, as

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:25.959
apposed to an anthropomorphic, or human-like,
god.

00:02:25.959 --> 00:02:32.030
Einstein was well known for his iconic
shabby look. Which consisted of wild, uncombed

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:39.720
hair and baggy, oversized clothes. Also he
never wore socks. He saw socks as unnecessary

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:45.060
and got frustrated that whenever he wore socks
he got holes in them. He wouldn’t even wear

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:48.670
socks or comb his hair when visiting the White
House.

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:53.920
Also part of Einstein’s “look” was
his pipe. Einstein loved to smoke, whether

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:58.819
it be cigarettes, cigars or his iconic pipe,
which was his favourite method of tobacco

00:02:58.819 --> 00:03:03.720
inhalation. When he walked between his house
and his office at Princeton University, he

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:09.250
would almost always be seen leaving behind
a trail of smoke. Einstein once had the following

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:14.239
to say on the matter: “I believe that pipe
smoking contributes to a somewhat calm and

00:03:14.239 --> 00:03:16.819
objective judgment in all human affairs.”

00:03:16.819 --> 00:03:22.959
It was well known by everyone that knew
him that Einstein had an incredibly bad memory.

00:03:22.959 --> 00:03:28.709
He couldn’t remember most people’s names
and couldn’t remember any phone numbers,

00:03:28.709 --> 00:03:29.569
including his own.

00:03:29.569 --> 00:03:35.269
In 1952, after Israel’s first President,
Israel Chaim Weizmann, died, Einstein was

00:03:35.269 --> 00:03:40.299
offered the position of Israel’s presidency,
because the Israelis believed him to be the

00:03:40.299 --> 00:03:48.110
greatest Jew alive. Einstein, then aged 73,
politely declined the offer. He said he lacked

00:03:48.110 --> 00:03:52.390
the “natural aptitude and the experience
to deal properly with people”.

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:57.680
Einstein used to charge people for his
autograph then donate all the money to charity.

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:04.299
Einstein was a prolific adulterer. During
his first marriage to Mileva Marić, Albert

00:04:04.299 --> 00:04:09.870
had at least six affairs with other women.
Knowing that his marriage was falling apart,

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:15.140
Einstein made one final attempt at keeping
the marriage together, for the sake of this

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:21.820
children. So what did he do exactly? He demanded
his wife signed a contract he drew up in order

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:26.550
to maintain the impression that they were
a happily married couple. The contract included

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:27.940
the following clauses:

00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:31.760
“You will make sure…
- that my clothes and laundry are kept in

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:35.550
good order;
- that I will receive my three meals regularly

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:37.300
in my room;

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:41.810
You will renounce all personal relations with
me insofar as they are not completely necessary

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:45.140
for social reasons. Specifically, you will
forego…

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:49.380
- my sitting at home with you;
- my going out or traveling with you.

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:52.890
You will obey the following points in your
relations with me…

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:58.260
- you will not expect any intimacy from me,
nor will you reproach me in any way;

00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:01.250
- you will stop talking to me if I request
it;

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:06.500
- you will leave my bedroom or study immediately
without protest if I request it.”

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:14.310
Way to be tactful Albert. Amazingly his wife
actually agreed to the terms, after much persuasion.

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:21.850
After he divorced Mileva Marić in 1919,
Einstein married his cousin, Elsa Loewenthal.

00:05:21.850 --> 00:05:28.070
She was very closely related to Einstein;
he was actually related to her on both sides

00:05:28.070 --> 00:05:33.680
of his family. They had played together as
kids but their romance didn’t flourish until

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:35.540
later on in their lives.

00:05:35.540 --> 00:05:41.500
Einstein’s favourite hobbies were sailing
and playing the violin. But neither came close

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:46.990
to his love for theoretical physics. Einstein
would play the violin to himself when he became

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:50.320
stuck in the thinking process whilst practicing
physics.

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:57.070
The prestigious Nobel Prize was awarded
to Albert Einstein in 1921. But not for his

00:05:57.070 --> 00:06:02.230
work on the theory of relativity. He actually
got it for his work on helping to discover

00:06:02.230 --> 00:06:08.530
the photoelectric effect. Which is the now,
well known phenomenon, that metals emit electrons

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:10.380
when light is shined upon them.

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:16.670
However all of Einstein’s Nobel Prize
money went to his ex-wife, Mileva, as a divorce

00:06:16.670 --> 00:06:17.310
settlement.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:23.830
About a week after Einstein died in 1955
at Princeton, before being cremated, an autopsy

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:29.050
was performed on his body by Thomas Harvey,
a pathologist at Princeton University. He

00:06:29.050 --> 00:06:35.310
removed Einstein’s brain for study, which
he intended to kept permanently as a keepsake

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:41.050
and personal research project. Harvey was
eventually fired from Princeton after refusing

00:06:41.050 --> 00:06:46.060
to hand over Einstein’s brain. After finding
it wasn’t any different to a normal brain,

00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:51.540
Harvey dissected it into over 200 pieces,
some of which he sent off to other researchers

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:56.780
for examination. It was eventually discovered
that Einstein’s parietal lobes, the parts

00:06:56.780 --> 00:07:02.850
of the brain responsible for mathematical,
visual and spatial cognition, were 15% larger

00:07:02.850 --> 00:07:04.340
than the average person’s.

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:10.140
Einstein’s brain was eventually transferred
and put on display at the Mütter Museum in

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:15.540
Philadelphia. His eye’s however were also
removed and handed to Henry Abrams, Einstein’s

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:21.100
eye doctor. To this day they remain in a safe
deposit box in New York City.

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:26.610
Einstein’s last words are not known
because he said them in German and the only

00:07:26.610 --> 00:07:29.940
person that heard them was a night nurse who
only spoke English.

00:07:29.940 --> 00:07:37.030
But all these facts pale in comparison
to the most amazing fact about Albert Einstein.

00:07:37.030 --> 00:07:42.690
In 1905 whilst working in Bern, Switzerland,
Einstein published a paper on his Special

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:47.820
Theory of Relativity”. Which challenged
the world’s idea of how space and time behaves

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:54.120
in the universe and set the tone of theoretical
physics for the next century, and counting.

00:07:54.120 --> 00:08:00.420
The ideas Einstein put forward in this revolutionary
paper had enormous consequences that completely

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:03.800
changed the way we think about, mass, energy,
space and time.

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:10.150
Oh and by the way, Einstein published
over 300 scientific papers over his lifetime.

00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:17.410
His paper on the Special Theory of Relativity
also included, what has become the most famous

00:08:17.410 --> 00:08:25.070
equation in the world, E=mc2, otherwise known
as the mass-energy equivalence. On a very

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:30.160
basic level it is the concept that the mass
of any object is a measure of how much energy

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:35.430
is contained within it. There were actually
numerous scientists who all claimed to have

00:08:35.430 --> 00:08:39.930
discovered the equation around the same time.
But it was eventually decided that Albert

00:08:39.930 --> 00:08:45.050
Einstein should be given the credit for it
as he put the most effort into its discovery.

00:08:45.050 --> 00:08:52.360
E=mc2 gave rise to the atomic bomb and
the nuclear arms race. Knowing that he was

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:57.490
mostly responsible for causing the atomic
bomb’s eventual discovery, Einstein slipped

00:08:57.490 --> 00:09:02.090
into a period of great depression. He believed
himself to be a pacifist.

00:09:02.090 --> 00:09:09.140
In 1915, Einstein completed his General
Theory of Relativity, which implied the existence

00:09:09.140 --> 00:09:15.170
of black holes and gravitational waves and
many other things, up until which point had

00:09:15.170 --> 00:09:21.120
been nothing more than hypotheses. Together
with his Special Theory of Relativity, Einstein’s

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:28.320
General Theory of Relativity formed the Theory
of Relativity. The cornerstone of modern physics

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:33.890
and arguably the most important discovery
in physics of the past century.

00:09:33.890 --> 00:09:38.800
Sure the Theory of Relativity is used
every day by physicists in their increasingly

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:45.610
complex endeavours. But its effects can be
seen in our everyday lives too. None of the

00:09:45.610 --> 00:09:51.260
following things would be possible without
Einstein’s two theories of relativity: GPS

00:09:51.260 --> 00:09:58.700
systems, televisions, nuclear power plants,
remote control devices, lasers, DVD-players

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:09.450
and many others. Oh and I nearly forgot to
mention, the universe itself.

